/** @page ncurses_quickstartguide Quick Start

    @tableofcontents

    @section ncursesquickstartsetup Terminal and Session

    Run interactive programs in a terminal with a valid \c TERM setting and a UTF-8 locale.
    Load the binary module with <tt>%requires ncurses</tt>, create a
    @ref Qore::Ncurses::Session "Session", and obtain its root surface with
    @ref Qore::Ncurses::Session::screen() "Session::screen()". Coordinates are zero-based:
    drawing methods take the row before the column.

    @ref Qore::Ncurses::Session::close() "Session::close()" restores the terminal. Register it
    with <tt>on_exit</tt> immediately after opening a session so exceptions also restore the terminal.
    Windows and panels belong to their session and must not be used after it closes.

    @section ncursesquickstartexample First Program

    Save this program as \c hello.qr and run <tt>qore --enable-debug hello.qr</tt>.
    It draws a greeting and waits for one input event:

    @code{.py}
%modern
%requires ncurses

Ncurses::Session session();
on_exit session.close();
Ncurses::Window window = session.screen();
window.clear();
window.drawText(1, 2, "Hello, Ncurses!", {
    "fg": Ncurses::Color::Cyan,
    "attrs": Ncurses::Attr::Bold,
});
window.drawText(3, 2, "Press a key to close");
window.refresh();
window.readEvent();
    @endcode

    @section ncursesquickstartinput Input and Next Steps

    @ref Qore::Ncurses::Window::readEvent() "Window::readEvent()" returns an
    @ref Qore::Ncurses::InputEvent "InputEvent" describing a character, special key, mouse action,
    or resize. With an explicit timeout it returns \c NOTHING when no event arrives;
    test the result before reading its fields. See @ref ncurses_mouseguide "Mouse Support"
    for an event loop and @ref ncurses_ui_widgetsguide "UI Widget Toolkit" for automatic dispatch.

    Session options control echo, raw/cbreak mode, mouse reporting, colors, and cursor visibility.
    The \c use_tty option opens a dedicated terminal device when standard output is being captured;
    see @ref Qore::Ncurses::Session::constructor() "Session options".
    For headless tests use @ref ncurses_testingguide "Automated Testing".
*/
